411
00:36:45,190 --> 00:36:49,270
I think whether it's a human, whether it's an agent, you know, whoever's consuming it.

412
00:36:49,270 --> 00:36:56,070
The thing is using a spec is is really just the most important part and using a a standard spec. So open API.

413
00:36:56,070 --> 00:37:00,310
So LLMs have been trained on like thousands and millions of examples of open API.

414
00:37:00,310 --> 00:37:08,630
So like you really do want to be using a well-known standard to be fed in because then you know whether it's a just a traditional computer or

415
00:37:08,630 --> 00:37:14,710
a human or an LLM probably going to get pretty good results because it's something that they're used to and they've been trained on.

416
00:37:14,710 --> 00:37:24,790
So, you know, I think that it could be a wash and, you know, I've seen people try and say that, oh, it doesn't matter as much because agents are pretty good at at dealing with, you know, bad APIs.

