00:37:34,069 --> 00:37:41,750
if you're playing around and you oh do a transactions API like there's kind of like the typical play APIs that you would make.

419
00:37:41,750 --> 00:37:49,990
you can make really bad versions of those APIs and the LLM has seen so many examples of it that it's really good at guessing what it's supposed to do.

420
00:37:49,990 --> 00:37:58,870
The problem lies in when you actually have a complex API with your own domain knowledge and logic that's not something that an LLM seen [clears throat] a million times.

